\fs36 \cf3 {\listtext	3.	}CJ01 linear air-inlet actuators + 2 \'d7 v3 inlet controllers (Items V.4\'96V.5)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf3 {\listtext	\'95	}Type: small-window push-rod (linear) actuator motor\
{\listtext	\'95	}Voltage: DC 24 V\
{\listtext	\'95	}Max current per unit at full load: 1.8 A\
{\listtext	\'95	}Peak power: 24 V \'d7 1.8 A \uc0\u8776  43.2 W (\u8776  43 W per our engineering documentation)\
{\listtext	\'95	}No-load running current: 0.4\'960.6 A (\uc0\u8776  10\'9615 W)\
{\listtext	\'95	}Duty cycle: short-time operation only \'97 the actuator strokes to position and then de-energizes, so standby consumption is negligible (relevant for your UPS sizing).\
{\listtext	\'95	}Connection: each actuator is driven by its paired v3 inlet controller.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf3 {\listtext	4.	}Power consumption (for UPS sizing)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf3 {\listtext	\'95	}DMR temperature/humidity sensor (each): DC 24 V, 0.8 W continuous, current \uc0\u8776  0.033 A\
{\listtext	\'95	}7-inch controller: we will confirm the exact figure with our technical team and advise you separately.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf3 {\listtext	5.	}Blackout-curtain drive motor The blackout-curtain you mention is the one on the small air-inlet window. There is no motor control on that shade \'97 it is not actuator-driven, so it neither shares a circuit nor spare parts with the inlet actuators.Also, there's no this item in the quotation!\uc0\u8232 \
\ls8\ilvl0{\listtext	6.	}Electrical single-line diagram / reference specification Sorry, our technical team normally issues the detailed electrical drawings after we received the advance payment. We will prepare the single-line diagram and reference specification for this installation at that stage.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls8\ilvl0{\listtext	7.	}Lighting layout Lighting is installed along the aisles (walkways). Each aisle carries 7 bulbs at 2.5 m spacing, with the positions shown in the attached lighting layout drawing. A back-to-back (double-sided) house therefore uses 14 bulbs in total \'97 exactly the quantity already in our quotation. No additional lighting is required; the quoted scheme already matches the current scale. As the complete lighting system is already covered, no additional dimming controller is needed.\uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0
