\fs32 \cf3 Dear Bety and FamTECH team,\
\'a0\
\'a0 Thank you very much for your detailed reply on ventilation and water/manure handling. That closes the design work we needed on that side for now \'97 the drawings in particular were a great help in finalizing some of our civil works planning.\
\'a0\
\'a0 Here is our third batch of questions, focused on the electrical specifications we need to finalize our panel and wiring design.\'a0\
\'a0\
\'a0 1. Power (kW/HP), voltage, and motor type (three-phase/single-phase) for the manure-removal belt motor (item III.2/III.4). This is the one motor not specified in any version of the quotation so far, and we need it to size the breaker and wiring for that circuit.\
\'a0 2. Rated current (A) and locked-rotor/starting current (LRA) for each quoted motor: feeder gearbox (0.75 kW), egg-belt motor (0.55 kW), and each of the two fans (1.1 kW). We need these values to size wire gauge, breakers, and contactors in our panel design.\
\'a0 3. Electrical specification (voltage, current, connection type) of the two CJ01 linear air-inlet actuators and their two inlet controllers (v3, items V.4\'96V.5). We need this to finish the wiring design for the air-inlet circuit.\
\'a0 4. Power consumption (W) of the YB controller (7\uc0\u8243 ) and of the DMR temperature/humidity sensors. We need this to size our backup power (UPS) capacity correctly.\
